    "intro_html":  "The name has nothing to do with weddings. It comes from the Italian \u003cem\u003eminestra maritata\u003c/em\u003e, the married soup, and the marriage in question is greens and meat. Little turkey meatballs, tender pasta shells, kale and spinach, all floating in a clean chicken broth with parmesan stirred in at the end. It is a soup that looks fancy in the container and costs less than a drive-through combo. That is the whole point of this operation.",
